/dsh-workbench-2.0.25-install.md

# Workbench captures and release artifacts. A screenshot taken to compare the plugin
# against its prototype is evidence for one session, not source, and it is never the
# thing the next change is read from. The packed tarball and the per-version install
# note stayed tracked through 2.9.26 and then stopped: the tarball is reproducible with
# `npm pack` from the same tree, and the note is a record of one machine's install, so
# both now live on the installing machine rather than in git or in `git status`.
.harness/
docs/prototypes/shots/
dsh-workbench/*.tgz
dsh-workbench/*-install.md

